    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Vilimoni Botitu's handling error hands France the bonus point before half-time",
          "body": "The turning point came before half-time, when Vilimoni Botitu, a late change to the starting XV after Isikeli Rabitu was reportedly sick, spilled the ball inside his own 22. France's Aaron Grandidier-Nkanang then secured the attacking bonus point, and the hosts led 26-3 at the break. Simione Kuruvoli's penalty was Fiji's only reward in the first half, and France's Kalvin Gourgues, on his first start for Les Bleus, went over in the corner 19 minutes into the second half."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22 with Henry Pollock scoring twice",
