        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Wallabies rout",
          "heading": "Henry Pollock scores twice on wing as England beat Australia 45-22",
          "body": "Henry Pollock, a back row Borthwick has identified as wing cover, crossed twice after replacing the injured Immanuel Feyi-Waboso at half-time. England's seven-try win answered a Times report claiming Borthwick presided over a toxic environment on the July tour. They conceded 15 yellow cards in their previous eight Tests of 2026 but none against Australia, and Henry Slade was named man of the match. Maro Itoje said afterwards: \"Steve is a world-class coach and we're lucky to have him.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France recall Marchand, Fickou and Carbonel for Springboks test",
          "body": "Wales: WRU formally bids for Premiership entry; URC threatens legal action. Argentina's Marcos Camerlinckx completes move to Bath Rugby."
        }
      ],
