    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Hooker's hat-trick",
          "heading": "Ewan Ashman hat-trick not enough as Scotland fail again against All Blacks",
          "body": "Ewan Ashman scored three first-half tries at Murrayfield, but the hooker's hat-trick left Scotland only three points down at the break before New Zealand ran in 19 unanswered second-half points. Scotland failed to score after the interval, and Gregor Townsend, the head coach, said: \"So that's frustrating.\" The Guardian's report called the defeat dispiritingly routine, with the Scots' first win over New Zealand still missing."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22 with Henry Pollock scoring twice",
