      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Anglo-Welsh talks",
          "heading": "WRU sends formal Premiership bid to RFU as URC threatens legal action",
          "body": "The WRU's letter asks the RFU for Welsh entry as the Premiership grows from 10 to 12 clubs, but the RFU currently say they are committed to English expansion, and the URC has threatened Wales with legal action. Former WRU chair Gareth Davies, speaking to S4C's Newyddion, floated a split in which two Welsh teams join the Premiership and two stay in the URC, calling that the best outcome Wales could get. He also warned that buying the shares needed could cost £40m."
        },
        {
