      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Transfer news",
          "heading": "Uncapped prop Marcos Camerlinckx completes move from Argentina to Bath Rugby",
          "body": "Bath have confirmed the signing of a 22-year-old whose move is his first professional experience outside South America. The move follows a Super Rugby Americas campaign in which he helped Los Pampas win their first title. He recently played for the Argentina XV against the USA and is on the radar for international duty despite being uncapped. His father, Pablo Camerlinckx, was a No. 8 for Los Pumas, debuting in 1989 and winning his final cap against Wales in 1999."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22 with Henry Pollock scoring twice",
