    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Test defeat",
          "heading": "Wallabies concede seven tries to England, with Jorgensen, Daugunu and Williams scoring",
          "body": "England ran in seven tries to beat the Wallabies 45-22 at Allianz Stadium, with Australia's scores coming from Max Jorgensen, Filipo Daugunu and Jeremy Williams. Jorgensen's intercept try had kept Australia within touching distance at half-time, but England led 19-10 at the break and Henry Pollock, who came on for the injured Immanuel Feyi-Waboso, scored twice after it. Gerard Meagher's Guardian verdict was that the Wallabies' set piece \"fell to pieces.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France recall Marchand, Fickou and Carbonel for Springboks test",
          "body": "Wales: WRU formally bids for Premiership entry; URC threatens legal action. Argentina's Marcos Camerlinckx completes move to Bath Rugby."
