    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Late rally",
          "heading": "Kenta Fukuda's late try not enough as Japan fall 28-21 to Wales",
          "body": "Japan trailed 21-14 at half-time in Cardiff on Saturday, having hit back through Warner Dearns' try, converted by Naoto Saito. A late try by replacement scrum-half Kenta Fukuda, converted by Shinya Komura, cut the gap to seven, but Wales held on. Josh Adams scored twice for Wales, who also had Archie Griffin's try inside three minutes and Louis Rees-Zammit his first try in eight internationals."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22 with Henry Pollock scoring twice",
